 2. ⛽️ Sub-$6 diesel 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: AAA; Chart: Ben Geman/Axios Average U.S. diesel prices inched below $6 per gallon today for the first time since Sept. 10, Axios' Ben Geman writes, citing AAA data . 

 The big picture: Diesel has soared even more than gasoline during the Iran war, and those costs rippled throughout the economy.

 🛢️ Yes, but: The global diesel supply crunch persists even as the broader oil market is starting to fitfully stabilize.

 Ukrainian attacks on Russian refineries, damage to Middle Eastern production and shipments, throttled oil supplies, and expanded U.S. exports to meet overseas demand helped raise domestic costs. Go deeper . 

 
 
